uit and she wore her  hair in a cutesy ponytail it wasn't  until later when the doll was redesigned  having more adult appearance she  received a complete makeover from her  facial expressions to her outfits there  are more Barbies than baby's born in the  US  during the first year of production more  than 350,000 Barbie dolls were sold  these days the doll is still one of the  most popular products in the toy  industry every second three Barbies are  sold around the world  that's 24 times more than the average  number of babies born in the United  States each year ken has never put a  ring on it  after meeting on the set of a television  commercial back in 1961 Barbie and Penny  became inseparable although they've had  a break up in some bumps along the way  the relationship has remained quite  solid throughout the years but despite  their history together in decades-long  romance the two have never been married  we think it's about time Ken puts a ring  on it how about you she keeps her makeup  simple although barbie has been known to  experiment with her look throughout the  years she likes to keep it simple when  it comes to her makeup her lipstick is  usually pink which is no surprise  considering it's her favorite color and  when it comes to her eyes the color  brown is most frequently used for her  eyeshadow she was banned in Saudi Arabia  you would think the iconic doll would be  embraced all over the globe but that's  simply not the case  Barbie was actually banned in Saudi  Arabia by the country's religious police  in 2003 the announcement was made that  the country declared the doll was an  immediate threat to morality due to for  revealing clothing not everyone sees her  as a role model the doll has come under  fire for her unrealistic body  proportions if Barbie were an actual  person she would be five nine she would  weigh a hundred and twenty pounds and  have a body measurement of 38 18:34 in  comparison the average woman has a body  measurement of 41